    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Clara Warden's individual podcast for PWR2: Sounds of Stanford. Explores the issues of irresponsible philanthropy--which is caused by what the author terms \"unproductive empathy\"--and the danger of giving without thinking. Highlights key issues of charitable giving including looking out for fraudulent charities, assessing the needs of those you are trying to help, and making sure the chosen intervention doesn't do more harm than good. Draws strongly upon interviews with Marci Stevens and Dr. Daryn Reicherter, on a case study on the Cancer Fund of America by the Center of Investigative Reporting, on material from the book Stones Into Schools by Greg Mortenson, and from theoretical texts in Taking Philanthropy Seriously, by Professor William Damon. For other sources see Works Cited at the end of Podcast Script",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
    ],
